          "type1": "<strong>Bipolar Type I</strong> — Characterised by manic episodes including euphoria, increased energy, and impulsive behaviours. Manic episodes can be preceded or followed by hypomanic or major depressive episodes.",
          "type2": "<strong>Bipolar Type II</strong> — Characterised by patterns of depressive episodes and hypomania, but without the full psychosis experience of bipolar I.",
